      "title": "Lecturer, Eldercare - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, ELDERCARE - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 25 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year position as a Lecturer, Eldercare in the School of Humanities and Interdisciplinary Studies. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Curriculum development, course delivery (face-to-face/online) and project supervision for youth and adult learners in the following areas: Perspectives of Ageing Empowerment & Wellness for Seniors Inclusive Ageing & Society Lifespan and Psychology of Ageing Gerontechnology and Behaviour Design Social Policy & Legislation in Ageing Population Health & Ageing Community Development for Seniors Intergenerational Service-Learning Multidisciplinary industry-based projects Able to teach at least one evening or weekends in the week Lead and identify new initiatives and collaborations with the industry, institutes of higher learnings & related agencies Stay updated on trends in community solution and care planning for seniors and integrates these into teaching and project work Handle administrative work relating to teaching and assigned projects Supervise students during internships What we are looking for Relevant tertiary qualification in Social Work, Community Development, Gerontology or equivalent Direct experience and strong interest in eldercare Experience in volunteer management, programme and project management in social, community and/or eldercare settings Experience in teaching communications related subjects and/or have IT skills will be an advantage An agile team player with good interpersonal and communication skills Proficient in project/time management with a keen attention to detail Connections within the non-profit, social service, or care sectors About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (AVIONICS) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (MECHANICAL) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, ELDERCARE - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
