      "title": "Service-Learning Catalyst, Lecturer - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 25 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year position as a Service-Learning Catalyst, Lecturer in the School of Humanities & Interdisciplinary Studies. We are seeking an experienced Service-Learning Educator to join our academic team in championing S-L as NP’s signature pedagogy across our academic faculty. This role involves building partnerships, mentoring faculty and students, and supporting research and innovation in Service-Learning.  The successful candidate will have a strong educational background, community engagement experience, and a proven ability to manage complex projects and foster collaborative relationships. The candidate must be prepared to teach and supervise projects for youth and adult learners. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Curriculum development, course delivery (face-to-face/online) and project supervision for youth and adult learners in the following areas: Social Sustainability Project Management & Multidisciplinary Collaborations Any of the module(s) offered in the School’s diploma programmes Plan, coordinate and facilitate implementation of Service-Learning modules across academic schools, ensuring alignment with diploma’s academic outcomes Provide Service-Learning training and mentorship on best practices to faculty both within the Polytechnic Establish and manage partnerships with internal and external stakeholders, including non-profits, government bodies, and corporations, to create meaningful Service-Learning projects Handle administrative tasks such as event publicity, data management, procurement, and other duties essential to the successful execution of Service-Learning programs, while also participating in broader institutional activities What we are looking for Passion for Service-Learning and community engagement Proven experience in Service-Learning pedagogy development and implementation Strong understanding of social innovation concepts, trends, and practices, with hands-on experience in social enterprise, non-profit management or social impact consulting Experience in establishing and sustaining partnerships with community and corporate organizations Relevant sector knowledge and experience in the arts, culture, media or community development – as offered in the school’s diploma programmes – will be an advantage About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytec