      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Software Engineering - School Of Infocomm Technology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM TECHNOLOGY Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 18 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in the School of InfoComm Technology. The school is looking for full-time lecturer to teach modules in the domain area of: - Software engineering - DevSecOps - Cloud services - Cloud deployment (Kubernetes, Terraform, etc) - Cloud architecture The candidate will be assigned to teach Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) classes in the area that he / she is a subject matter expert in. Training will be provided for domain areas that candidates are unfamiliar with. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Develop teaching and assessment materials, conduct lessons and facilitate learning for both the PET and CET learners Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum. This includes regular review of existing curriculum and making recommendations on areas of improvement that would enhance students’ learning, performance, and employability. Keep abreast of current trends and developments in technologies and emerging trends Handle administrative work relating to teaching. Supervise and mentor students in competitions and consultancy projects Support student learning through consultation and mentorship Identify and establish new collaboration opportunities with industry partners for curriculum collaboration, CET programme initiatives, and consultancy projects Work on industry or consultancy projects Organise and lead overseas study trips, immersion programs, and student exchange initiatives What we are looking for At least 3 years of relevant working experience in software engineering, DevSecOps, terraform, cloud services and/or deployment. Committed to stay updated with industry advancements and integrating new technologies into teaching. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring both youths and adult learners. Ability to design engaging curriculum, developing materials and delivering classes. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. Possess wit, innovation, initiative and strong communication skills. Relevant professional certifications will have added advantage, e.g. Kubernetes Application Developer, OpenShift Administrator, AWS Solutions Architect, Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMO