      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer – Emotional Intelligence & Global Citizenship - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSHIP - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 25 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, Emotional Intelligence & Global Citizenship in the School of Humanities & Interdisciplinary studies. What you will be working on We are looking for an educator-facilitator who believes that developing the inner world of young people is an important part of preparing them for the outer world . This role sits at the intersection of emotional intelligence, interpersonal communication and global perspectives.  You will design and facilitate learning experiences that help young people better understand themselves, relate meaningfully to others, and think critically about the role they play in the world as agents of change.  As a facilitator of learning, you will guide students to discover their purpose and values, explore diverse perspectives on global issues, and translate their learning into meaningful community action. Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Facilitate engaging learning experiences for youths and adult learners focused on: Emotional Intelligence and Self-awareness Interpersonal Communication and Collaboration Creativity and Problem Solving Critical Thinking and Global Awareness Mentor youths (typically aged 16–20) through guided reflection, dialogue, experiential and project-based learning Design and facilitate learning experiences that connect classroom inquiry to real-world contexts, including community-based projects, civic dialogue or applied problem-solving Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to continuously refine curriculum and learning experiences Provide pastoral care and holistic support for student development Able to teach at least one evening or weekends in the week Manage administrative work related to teaching and assigned projects Take on leadership roles in module delivery or project teams, , including study trips where required Undertake academic‑related administration, committee work, outreach activities, and ad‑hoc projects that support the School’s mission What we are looking for A relevant tertiary qualification, with at least 3 years of teaching and/or industry experience in Arts & Humanities, Business, Design, or related fields A strong belief in holistic education and the development of human skills, including emotional intelligence, communication, creative and critical thinking Experience in mentoring, coaching or working with youths Strong facilitation, interpersonal and communication skills Ability to design and facilitate engaging, interactive and reflective learning experiences Strong organisational skills, with attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities A reflective practitioner who is open to learning, experimenting, and growing It would be an advantage if you have: Training or experience in areas such as emotional intelligence, youth development and/or global education Experience in facilitating civic dialogue or leading community-based learning projects About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, ELDERCARE - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (AVIONICS) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (MECHANICAL) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSHIP - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17708288/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b0d1-9ee03d7a140b": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Aerospace Engineering (Mechanical) - School Of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (MECHANICAL) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 25 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer, Aerospace Engineering (Mechanical) in the School of Engineering. We are seeking experienced aerospace professionals to join our Aerospace Engineering team as Lecturers specializing in aircraft mechanical systems. The successful candidate will teach core aerospace engineering modules, develop industry-relevant curriculum, and support student development through mentoring, industry projects, and overseas learning opportunities. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Develop, deliver, and assess aerospace-related adult learning courses and diploma modules, aligned with industry needs and focused on practical and experiential learning. Monitor and guide student progress and learning outcomes in modules, projects, and workplace learning activities. Build and maintain industry partnerships to identify and spearhead new opportunities and collaborations with industry. Support course management team in curriculum review, development and other administrative tasks Support student development in the area of education, including serving as advisor for students and leading overseas trips Participate in pedagogical training, and keep updated with industry developments and trends Work on industry or consultancy project to stay relevant in your profession. Lead or support applied R&D projects in collaboration with industry partners, focusing on technology development for aerospace industry. What we are looking for Degree in Aerospace/Mechanical Engineering or equivalent Experience with aircraft maintenance, aerospace engineering, airline operations and MRO environments Strong knowledge of aircraft mechanical systems, propulsion systems, aircraft structures, and maintenance practices Passionate about education and possess strong interest in nurturing, teaching, mentoring and interacting with students. Experience in training/mentoring would be an advantage. CAAS B1 licence would be an advantage. Good communication and interpersonal skills. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, ELDERCARE - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (AVIONICS) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (MECHANICAL) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17896195/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-af88-6d77a74b140b": {
      "title": "Skills Manager (Contract Till 6 Jul 2028) - Cet Academy",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SKILLS MANAGER (CONTRACT TILL 6 JUL 2028) - CET ACADEMY Ngee Ann Polytechnic 07-10 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 18 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a contract position till 6 Jul 2028 as a Skills Manager in the CET Academy. We are seeking a motivated and experienced professional to lead the identification, development, and assessment of workforce skills required to support organisational performance. The role involves working closely with internal stakeholders and external partners across multiple sectors to drive skills development initiatives, support workforce transformation, and strengthen industry capability. The successful candidate will collaborate with various departments and partner organisations to recommend and implement relevant training programmes that address emerging skills needs and contribute to organisational and industry growth. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Skills Assessment Conduct skills gap analysis to determine current competencies versus required skills. Use assessments, surveys and interviews to evaluate employees’ skills level. Diagnose learning gaps and needs,and identify measurements of success. Programme Development Design and implement training programmes to enhance employees skills and competencies. Use Skills Frameworks and SkillsFuture resources to create learning solutions and learning interventions. Work with various schools as well as Academic Partners to co-develop customised learning solutions and interventions. Manage, coordinate and execute programmes for SMEs, and other products from various schools. Work internally and externally to obtain Government funding for training programmes, where applicable. Develop implementation plan and drive adoption. Training Coordination Organise workshops, seminars, and training sessions. Engage with various Schools and Academic Partners for suitable trainers. Drive strategy and tactics to ensure conversions across all platforms and channels. Programme launch and events management. Performance Monitoring Track and evaluate the effectiveness of training programmes and initiatives. Maintain records of employee progress and skill development. Track return on investment on training for clients. Reporting Prepare reports on skills assessments and training outcomes for management review. Evaluate impact and effectiveness of training interventions. Provide recommendations for further training and development opportunities. Continuous Improvements Stay up-to-date with industry trends and best practices in skills development and training. Lead research on industry landscape and market trends to understand critical skills requirements and future skills demand. Advocate for a culture of continuous learning and professional development. What we are looking for Bachelor’s Degree in a relevant field (e.g. Business Administration, Human Resource, Marketing or any related field) At least 7 - 10 years of relevant experience in learning and development, business development, account management, events or project management Effective communication, interpersonal and project management skills to collaborate with diverse stakeholders Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, and ability to interpret data for decision-making Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (word, excel, powerpoint), project management tools, and prior experience in learning development and account management for SMEs would be an advantage Proven experience in training management or similar roles, preferably with knowledge of CET training Ability to work independently and manage multiple projects in a hybrid work environment Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment *Applicants should note that their curriculum vitae (CV) and relevant application information may be shared with authorised external partner agencies and third parties involved in the recruitment, assessment and selection process. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in [Intern] EXCEL & Advisory Programmes MND Closing on 31 Dec 2026 L&D Specialist (Service and Operations Management), IPAM CSC Closing on 31 Oct 2026 Manager (Training Excellence) Civil Aviation Authority Of Singapore Closing on 21 Oct 2026 Manager (Training Support) People'S Association Closing in 5  day(s) Senior/Principal Manager (Digital Learning Technologist) Building And Construction Authority Closing in 6  day(s) Manager (Training & Learning Development - Cyber) - Stagmont MINDEF DXO Closing on 28 Oct 2026 Snr Exec/Dy Mgr - Mentoring & Integrated Care Mgmt [ITE Headquarters] Institute Of Technical Education Closing on 19 Oct 2026 Deputy Manager - Data Analysis & Surveys [ITE Headquarters] – 2 Year C Institute Of Technical Education Closing on 19 Oct 2026 SKILLS MANAGER (CONTRACT TILL 6 JUL 2028) - CET ACADEMY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18089054/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-aea3-d2f5c754340b": {
      "title": "Project Engineer (11-Month Contract) - School Of Infocomm Technology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button PROJECT ENGINEER (11-MONTH CONTRACT) - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM TECHNOLOGY Ngee Ann Polytechnic 01-03 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 2  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is an 11-month contract position as a Project Engineer in the School of InfoComm Technology. The Project Engineer supports the AI and Digitalisation Centre (AIDC) by developing and maintaining internal AI, automation, software, systems-integration and digitalisation capabilities. The role focuses on building reusable prototypes, technical assets, demonstration platforms and internal digital tools while supporting technology research, testing, documentation and technical implementation. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Develop and maintain AI, automation, software, systems-integration and digitalisation solutions for the AI and Digitalisation Centre (AIDC). Build reusable technical assets, proof-of-concept templates, demonstration systems, workflow automations, dashboards, API connectors and deployment patterns for future use. Conduct technical research, feasibility studies, testing, benchmarking and experimentation on relevant AI and digitalisation technologies. Support AIDC internal digitalisation including workflow automation, knowledge management, document processing, enquiry tracking, reporting and operational tools. Maintain AIDC development, test and demonstration environments including technical documentation, code repositories, system configurations and implementation guides. Support technical planning, issue tracking, quality testing and continuous improvement for internal AIDC initiatives. Provide limited early-stage technical input for opportunity exploration, including demonstrations, high-level feasibility assessments and non-binding solution concepts. What we are looking for Diploma or Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a related discipline. At least 1 year of relevant hands-on experience in software development, systems integration, automation, digitalisation, AI-enabled solutions or technical project implementation. Proficiency in at least one programming or scripting language, such as Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, Go, Java, or equivalent. Familiarity with developing web applications, APIs, databases, workflow automations, dashboards, cloud services or on-premises systems. Basic knowledge of AI and generative AI concepts. Familiarity with Git-based version control, testing, technical documentation, issue tracking and deployment practices. Ability to analyze operational needs and translate them into practical technical solutions. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, documentation, communication and problem-solving skills. Demonstrates initiative, adaptability, attention to detail and a willingness to learn and experiment with emerging technologies. Advantageous Requirements, Preferred but not a need Experience with Docker, Linux, cloud platforms such as AWS or Azure, networking, authentication, access control and data-security practices. Experience with deploying or integrating AI applications, APIs, databases, cloud services and enterprise systems. Familiarity with DevOps, CI/CD, containerization, system monitoring or infrastructure-as-code practices. Experience developing proof-of-concept systems, technical demonstrations, automation workflows, IoT applications, dashboards, computer-vision solutions, or internal digital tools. Experience supporting technical projects from planning and prototyping through testing, documentation, deployment and handover Possession of or progress towards a recognized project-management certification such as Project Management Professional (PMP), Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM), Scrum Master or an equivalent certification. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in Deputy Director, AI R&D (LLM & Multimodal AI), Q Team CoE HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Head, Cyber Threat Intelligence, Tech Ops, xCyber HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Lead Engineer/Engineer, Security-By-Design, CISO Office, xCyber HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Lead Engineer / Engineer (Product Management), Content Platform, xDigi HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Lead Engineer / Engineer, AI Agent Engineer, Programme Planning Office HTX Closing in 6  day(s) Intern, Digital Media, CED MOM Closing on 17 Oct 2026 Snr/Asst Director, Cyber Crisis Preparedness, Technology & Logistics P HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Head, Cyber Development & Research, AI Security & Research, xCyber HTX Closing on 16 Oct 2026 PROJECT ENGINEER (11-MONTH CONTRACT) - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM TECHNOLOGY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18089057/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-aea3-d5328af1540b": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Admin - Digital Services & Technology Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SENIOR EXECUTIVE, ADMIN - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 2  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract for an Senior Executive, Admin position with the Digital Services & Technology Office. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Manage Assets in accordance with FIN’s policies and procedures, e.g. annual Physical Verification Exercise, Low-Value Asset Declaration, Write-off and Disposal of Assets, AUC conversion to Fixed Assets in the system Lead the annual Asset Physical Verification Exercise. Review and oversee the bi-annual asset disposal exercises. Manage procurement approval for AOR, QAA, Variation & Small Value Purchases (SVP) Manage Master Procurement Records/CC Portal, email-in of SVP, direct billing, Purchase Order (PO) Details Assist with collation of data for internal and external returns to Finance Office and other government agencies. Review and implement improvement to internal procurement and administrative processes Assist with General Office Administration as a Covering Officer during colleague’s absence. What we are looking for Experience in fixed assets management and annual physical verification exercise Experience in admin and procurement in Schools / Admin Departments in Institutes of Higher Learning is an advantage Effective team player who can collaborate and complete tasks efficiently as a team Initiative to work on improvements to own job areas as well as contribute actively to the Team’s overall performance Meticulous, strong admin skills, able to multi-task and complete tasks assigned with a sense of urgency Good spoken and written English and communication skills is a must Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, Outlook), SharePoint, and OneDrive IT savvy with prior experience in automation and a drive for innovation and continuous improvement initiatives to enhance operational efficiency Proficiency in the use of AI tools is a plus Able to work with different stakeholders within Department especially with Finance Office. Eager to learn and grow with Digital Services & Technology Office About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in Senior/Assistant Director (Procurement) METI- HQ Closing on 06 Nov 2026 Manager/Assistant Director (Planning), Community Relations Unit MND Closing on 18 Oct 2026 Executive/Manager (IDD1) [Temp - 6 Mths] Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing in 5  day(s) [LTA-PP] DEPUTY/ASSISTANT MANAGER, POLICY (PRIVATE TRANSPORT) Land Transport Authority Closing on 29 Oct 2026 [LTA-VS] PRINCIPAL / SENIOR  EXECUTIVE, HEAVY VEHICLE PARKING Land Transport Authority Closing on 21 Oct 2026 Assistant Manager/Manager, Procurement, Assurance & Corporate Excellen Sport Singapore Closing in 6  day(s) Office of the Registrar - Assistant Manager (Admissions Systems) Republic Polytechnic Closing on 29 Oct 2026 Office of the Registrar - Manager (Admissions) Republic Polytechnic Closing on 29 Oct 2026 SENIOR EXECUTIVE, ADMIN - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18089066/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-aea3-d6fcb019f40b": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Cet Outreach & Business Devt (11-Mth Contract) - Sch Of Ict",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SENIOR EXECUTIVE, CET OUTREACH & BUSINESS DEVT (11-MTH CONTRACT) - SCH OF ICT Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 2  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is an 11-month contract position as a Senior Executive in the School of InfoComm Technology. We are looking for a driven and organised CET Outreach & Business Development Senior Executive to support the growth of our Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes. This role focuses on outreach, lead management, and conversion, as well as cross-selling relevant CET offerings to corporate clients and individuals. The successful candidate will work closely with programme teams and trainers to move prospects from initial engagement through to enrolment, while building longer-term relationships with industry partners. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Outreach & Lead Generation Conduct targeted outreach to companies, public agencies, and individuals to promote CET programmes. Support marketing and engagement activities (events, briefings, info sessions, industry touchpoints). Work with marketing colleagues to support targeted campaigns, including messaging, publicity channels, outreach lists, and follow-up. Maintain outreach pipelines and ensure timely follow-ups. Lead Management & Conversion Manage incoming leads across multiple channels (email, events, referrals, enquiries). Qualify leads and guide them through the engagement and decision-making process. Coordinate with internal stakeholders to respond to client needs and close enrolments. Track lead status, conversion rates, and follow-up actions. Cross-Selling & Account Development Identify opportunities to cross-sell or upsell relevant CET courses and programmes based on client needs. Support relationship management with existing corporate clients to encourage repeat training engagements. Work with programme teams to propose suitable learning pathways and bundled offerings. Coordination & Reporting Liaise with academic, administrative, and marketing teams to ensure smooth client experience. Prepare basic reports on outreach activities, pipeline status, and conversion outcomes. Support continuous improvement of outreach and engagement processes. Interested candidates should note that the role involves weekend and evening support, with estimated frequency of twice a month on average. In addition to the above, other ad hoc duties may also be assigned. What we are looking for Experience in outreach, sales support, client management, training administration, or business development, in the area of lifelong learning, workforce development, or continuing education. Experience in marketing campaign support or promotional outreach would be an advantage. Strong follow-up discipline, organisational skills, and attention to detail. Comfortable engaging external stakeholders and handling multiple leads concurrently. Able to communicate clearly and professionally with corporate and public-sector clients, as well as individuals. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in Manager, Logistics & Supply Chain Management Economic Development Board Closing on 29 Oct 2026 Senior Associate/Manager, Chemicals and Materials Economic Development Board Closing on 29 Oct 2026 Communications & Engagement (National Cybersecurity Campaign) Intern, MDDI-CSA Closing on 31 Oct 2026 Assistant Director, Tech & Industry Lead (AMR/Robotics) Info-Communications Media Development Au Closing on 30 Dec 2026 HR Employer Branding Intern, CSA MDDI-CSA Closing on 31 Oct 2026 (Senior) Development Partner, Food Manufacturing Enterprise Singapore Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Assistant Director, Marketing Sport Singapore Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Contract Assistant Manager/Manager, Business Technology Partnerships ( Singapore Tourism Board Closing on 22 Oct 2026 SENIOR EXECUTIVE, CET OUTREACH & BUSINESS DEVT (11-MTH CONTRACT) - SCH OF ICT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18108684/005056a3-d347-1fe1-afba-b68d4eb322bf": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Student Finance Operations - Finance Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SENIOR EXECUTIVE, STUDENT FINANCE OPERATIONS - FINANCE OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 02-04 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 18 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Senior Executive in the Finance Office. The Senior Finance Executive is responsible for supporting student finance operations, including billing, fee collection administration, bank reconciliations, financial assistance scheme processing, student refunds, and financial record management. The incumbent will manage and respond to enquiries from both internal and external stakeholders, provide supporting financial documentation, and oversee communications through the common student finance email mailbox. The role requires the ability to handle a high volume of enquiries and transactions efficiently, ensuring accurate and timely resolution within established service standards and deadlines. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: 1. Student Finance Operations Manage student finance operations throughout the student lifecycle, including fee billing, collections, student account maintenance, adjustments, and refunds. Administer sponsorship arrangements, financial schemes and education loan schemes, including billing, collections, repayments, organization account maintenance and reconciliation activities. Prepare and issue student finance communications, including fee vouchers, financial scheme information and outstanding fee reminders. Manage and update student finance digital resources, including websites, FAQs, instructional videos, and the Fin_Student mailbox. Perform bank reconciliation and monitor student-related collection activities to ensure timely and accurate receipting and follow-up of outstanding items. Maintain accurate records and documentation to support reporting, governance, audit, and operational requirements. Handle any other duties as assigned from time to time. 2. Stakeholder Management Handle enquiries from students, parents, organisations, external and internal stakeholders, including financial assistance, fee-related matters and complex cases requiring review and follow-up. Work closely with departments and organisations to advise and resolve student related matters. Respond to audit queries and provide supporting documentation. 3. Process Improvement & Digitalisation Support system upgrades and digitalisation projects, including testing, implementation and change management. Participate in process improvement, automation and system enhancement initiatives to improve service delivery, productivity and operational effectiveness. What we are looking for Minimum 2 years of relevant experience in finance, accounts receivable, student finance, or administrative operations will be an advantage. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel, Word and Powerpoint. Good interpersonal and communication skills, with a customer service-oriented mindset. Good problem-solving skills in identifying issues, assess information and follow through to resolution. Ability to handle high-volume transactions accurately and efficiently . Able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment and manage competing priorities during peak periods. Familiarity with bank reconciliation processes and financial transaction analysis. Open to learning and adopting new technologies and digital solutions, and innovative work practices to drive continuous improvement and enhance customer service. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in Executive/Snr Executive/Asst Director, Finance (Project Evaluation) MOT Closing in 6  day(s) Senior Officer/ Executive, Finance PMO- NRF Closing in 5  day(s) Admin & Finance Officer - SPF/ CID MHA- SPF Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Senior Section Manager / Section Manager, Credit Management Services MOF- Vital Closing in 5  day(s) Senior Executive - Finance Department Nanyang Polytechnic Closing on 26 Oct 2026 [LTA-PT] DEPUTY/ ASSISTANT MANAGER, BUS OPERATIONS (BOS) Land Transport Authority Closing on 29 Oct 2026 Associate/Assistant Director, Financial Advisers Supervision Monetary Authority Of Singapore Closing in 5  day(s) AI Risk Management Supervision, Division Head Monetary Authority Of Singapore Closing in 5  day(s) SENIOR EXECUTIVE, STUDENT FINANCE OPERATIONS - FINANCE OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
    }
  },
